From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:24:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep baked module bindings live and cache stable conversions

1. Live module bindings: an export of a pre-bundled chunk can be
   undefined until its __esm init runs, so each read keeps consulting
   the host namespace. One host pin per export holds the last raw host
   value, and its marker holds the matching Boa conversion. The
   conversion is reused only while Object.is reports SameValue, so
   Promise and object identity survive without making exports stale.
   Markers are only stored as module exports, so ordinary name reads
   do not pay for the host lookup.
2. Non-recursive Debug for Module and IndirectBinding, so cyclic ES
   imports (A imports B imports A) don't overflow the stack in the
   derived formatter.

Assignment that resolves to an indirect (re-exported) module binding
should throw a catchable TypeError, but ModuleEnvironment::set cannot
report one. Drop the write instead of panicking through the embedder
boundary. The correct upstream fix is to throw a TypeError.
